      <pubDate>Mon, 16 Nov 2026 08:39:04 +0000</pubDate>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;We've had  extremely light weight versions of this for ages in &lt;a href="https://chaos.social/tags/rocq" class="mention hashtag" rel="nofollow noopener" target="_blank"&gt;#&lt;span&gt;rocq&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;. Some tactics (e.g. auto) are basically trying to auto-generate proofs. Actually having some sort of AI generated and simplified proof would probably be more informative than `Proof. auto. Qed.` Letting a computer check that the invariants hold while we do the useful work. Thoughts on that? Pitchforks?&lt;/p&gt;</description>
